WEBVTT

00:00:01.281 --> 00:00:13.159
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.932
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:25.861
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:37.376
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:43.523
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:50.929
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.739
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:05.612
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.612 --> 00:01:11.218
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:17.491
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.491 --> 00:01:25.921
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:30.203 --> 00:01:32.467
What's the matter?

00:01:39.112 --> 00:01:40.704
Palza!

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:47.687
Why didn't you come?

00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:49.952
Now, let's go.

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:54.791
You're not actually thinking about
staying here, are you?

00:01:55.662 --> 00:01:58.130
What if I am thinking that?!

00:01:58.932 --> 00:02:03.369
I can't take this anymore!
I want to stay here!

00:02:05.172 --> 00:02:07.741
What's brought this on
all of a sudden, Palza?

00:02:07.741 --> 00:02:10.310
Sudden?!
You call this sudden?!

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.547
This isn't sudden! You should
all know what this is about!

00:02:13.547 --> 00:02:16.539
What we did was wrong!

00:02:16.817 --> 00:02:21.154
I'm tired of it.
I want to stay here.

00:02:21.154 --> 00:02:23.990
I am Conrad Rugen!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:26.493
Coward! Traitor!

00:02:26.493 --> 00:02:29.758
What's going to happen
to me with you gone?!

00:02:30.063 --> 00:02:31.928
I'm begging you, Palza!

00:02:32.098 --> 00:02:37.627
Palza, no matter what your feelings,
we can't just accept that.

00:02:37.871 --> 00:02:40.032
-Stand up, Palza!
-Conrad!

00:02:40.507 --> 00:02:42.099
Conrad!

00:02:43.009 --> 00:02:45.011
- Conrad!
- Mama!

00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:48.606
- Conrad!
- Mama! Mama!

00:03:11.938 --> 00:03:13.838
Goodbye, Conrad...

00:03:14.574 --> 00:03:16.974
Conrad Rugen.

00:03:18.979 --> 00:03:22.916
Our journey in search of a girl who was
reincarnated every hundred years...

00:03:22.916 --> 00:03:25.282
continued on.

00:03:25.819 --> 00:03:28.955
However, in the year 1853,

00:03:28.955 --> 00:03:33.026
we lost one of our friends, Palza, here.

00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:33.693
THE PATH
we lost one of our friends, Palza, here.

00:03:33.693 --> 00:03:34.861
THE PATH

00:03:34.861 --> 00:03:37.864
THE PATH
This event was to have
a major impact on us.

00:03:37.864 --> 00:03:39.695
This event was to have
a major impact on us.

00:03:46.573 --> 00:03:48.302
Found it.

00:03:55.181 --> 00:03:58.776
The record of the memories
we extracted during our last year.

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:00.948
Aghi.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:07.060
Hasmodye.
Here, Tarlant.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.187
I don't really need it though.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.859
Even without relying on this thing,
I am always myself.

00:04:17.737 --> 00:04:20.171
It's them! They're here!

00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:26.912
Enma. They have always been
chasing after us.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.247
They're trying to make
us forget our mission.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:34.718
We've had to keep
fighting them all this time.

00:06:11.084 --> 00:06:13.186
Don't be afraid, Hasmodye.

00:06:13.186 --> 00:06:15.088
They'll see into your heart.

00:06:15.088 --> 00:06:18.182
They are always looking for us.

00:06:28.568 --> 00:06:30.270
Is this the Cole residence?

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:31.438
Who are you?

00:06:31.438 --> 00:06:34.703
My name is Cooks.
I'm with the State Police.

00:06:35.909 --> 00:06:37.638
A detective?

00:06:39.212 --> 00:06:40.941
I see...

00:06:41.281 --> 00:06:43.917
So it isn't that you've found Ian, is it?

00:06:43.917 --> 00:06:47.284
This is a group known as
the Children of Befort.

00:06:49.322 --> 00:06:51.153
Befort?

00:06:51.224 --> 00:06:54.022
This looks like a really old picture.

00:07:06.406 --> 00:07:08.931
This is a picture of Ian, isn't it?

00:07:09.175 --> 00:07:12.110
What do you think?
They look a lot alike, don't they?

00:07:16.449 --> 00:07:18.752
Are you saying that this is Ian?

00:07:18.752 --> 00:07:22.779
No, this picture was taken
more than 100 years ago.

00:07:23.623 --> 00:07:26.387
It can't possibly be your son.

00:07:28.128 --> 00:07:30.323
I see...

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:35.667
However, I can't help
wondering about this picture.

00:07:40.673 --> 00:07:43.665
You've been living in this hotel
for the past 6 years, right?

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.473
I only come back to sleep.
It's pretty messy.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.519
Who are you?!

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.192
Is this all you have?

00:07:59.192 --> 00:08:00.260
What?!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:03.821
After all this time, is this all that
you've managed to find?

00:08:03.963 --> 00:08:07.694
What's this about?!
Do you know those children?!

00:08:09.068 --> 00:08:12.663
They're evil, hateful monsters.

00:08:15.041 --> 00:08:17.032
Don't move!

00:08:23.683 --> 00:08:25.150
Damn it!

00:08:27.353 --> 00:08:29.583
Yahoo!

00:08:43.436 --> 00:08:45.199
It's a boat.

00:08:48.308 --> 00:08:50.299
Chikao?

00:08:52.879 --> 00:08:57.782
In the year 2012, Thoma from Papin
Island meets the orphan Helga.

00:08:58.551 --> 00:09:01.679
As if something pulled them together.

00:09:02.322 --> 00:09:05.314
Thoma's journey began here.

00:09:06.392 --> 00:09:08.661
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:09:08.661 --> 00:09:11.164
A boat on the shore has
the name "Chikao" on it.

00:09:11.164 --> 00:09:13.155
Is that where you came from?

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:17.965
Hey! I know you can hear me!
You could at least answer me!

00:09:21.074 --> 00:09:23.243
What's with her? Fine, whatever...

00:09:23.243 --> 00:09:25.912
There are poisonous snakes
and killer bees around here.

00:09:25.912 --> 00:09:28.107
If you get bit you'll die!

00:09:34.721 --> 00:09:37.383
You'd better go back home
before sunset!

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:51.430
I'm sorry to have caused
you all this trouble. Well...

00:10:11.124 --> 00:10:12.492
Who's that girl?

00:10:12.492 --> 00:10:14.928
They said she ran away
from the orphanage.

00:10:14.928 --> 00:10:17.430
Your father found her all by herself
on the south shore,

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.265
so he contacted them right away.

00:10:19.265 --> 00:10:20.900
Did you ask why?
Why'd she do it?!

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:23.269
Well, I'm sure she must
have had a reason.

00:10:23.269 --> 00:10:26.295
But we still had to
contact them, Thoma.

00:10:32.512 --> 00:10:35.415
In order to save Helga, who was being
mistreated by the orphanage director,

00:10:35.415 --> 00:10:37.583
together with Chitto from
the same orphanage,

00:10:37.583 --> 00:10:40.381
Thoma headed for Chikao Island.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.923
What the?

00:10:52.932 --> 00:10:54.832
It wasn't my fault!

00:10:57.337 --> 00:10:58.638
Helga!

00:10:58.638 --> 00:11:01.163
Chitto, you're all right.

00:11:02.041 --> 00:11:03.872
I'm so glad.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.777
Hey, Chitto!

00:11:09.182 --> 00:11:12.117
Helga, this is Thoma from
Papin Island.

00:11:13.353 --> 00:11:16.447
With all this confusion we should
be able to get away now. Let's go!

00:11:23.529 --> 00:11:27.488
This... You drew this?

00:11:28.001 --> 00:11:32.062
It's the place Helga wants to go.
I've decided to take her there.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.205
I've seen this somewhere before.

00:11:43.449 --> 00:11:46.486
Somewhere on the islands around here.
Right, Mom?

00:11:46.486 --> 00:11:51.124
Really? But there's no
place like this around here.

00:11:51.124 --> 00:11:52.921
Is this a building?

00:11:54.627 --> 00:11:58.364
Well, if it's not a building...
Is it some kind of machine?

00:11:58.364 --> 00:12:00.199
That's dumb, Mom!

00:12:00.199 --> 00:12:02.368
There are no machines like that!

00:12:02.368 --> 00:12:06.305
Helga is looking for a place!
A place! Right, Helga?

00:12:06.305 --> 00:12:08.330
Do you recognize it, honey?

00:12:10.209 --> 00:12:11.978
There's just not much to go on.

00:12:11.978 --> 00:12:15.581
What do you mean?! This is
something very important to Helga!

00:12:15.581 --> 00:12:18.880
Take it more seriously!
Here, your tools.

00:12:29.996 --> 00:12:31.931
Take that!

00:12:31.931 --> 00:12:34.991
Cut it out, Thoma!

00:13:19.378 --> 00:13:21.514
They said that the old
man holed up in there

00:13:21.514 --> 00:13:24.608
released a powerful electric charge
and killed one person.

00:13:29.288 --> 00:13:32.883
T-This response is...
I-It's Orsel!

00:13:34.927 --> 00:13:37.054
What did you say?!

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:39.165
The waveform of Orsel.

00:13:39.165 --> 00:13:42.430
Orsel doesn't exist anywhere in nature,

00:13:42.635 --> 00:13:45.571
only in the Zone.
It can't be!

00:13:45.571 --> 00:13:47.562
Let's check it out!

00:13:48.975 --> 00:13:50.676
What we saw in there was

00:13:50.676 --> 00:13:54.612
a mysterious old man who was
emitting Orsel from his body.

00:13:55.481 --> 00:13:58.041
Why was Orsel coming from his body?

00:13:59.485 --> 00:14:02.045
Who are you people?

00:14:03.956 --> 00:14:07.858
The light coming from your body
is not ordinary electricity!

00:14:09.629 --> 00:14:12.698
Orsel. It's the light you're emitting.

00:14:12.698 --> 00:14:16.302
I don't know! I don't understand this!

00:14:16.302 --> 00:14:19.100
What did you do?!
What was done to you?!

00:14:22.408 --> 00:14:24.544
Did you open the Zone?

00:14:24.544 --> 00:14:27.843
The Zone?
What are you talking about?

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:31.575
Our mission was to test
an aviation machine.

00:14:31.751 --> 00:14:35.050
I just did what the people from
the organization told me to do.

00:14:36.856 --> 00:14:38.551
Kirchner!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.449
Kirchner!

00:15:23.836 --> 00:15:26.168
Kirchner...

00:15:33.179 --> 00:15:35.147
He disappeared.

00:15:43.289 --> 00:15:45.018
Who are you?

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:53.666
That old man named Kirchner,

00:15:53.666 --> 00:15:56.032
he said he was put on board
a machine.

00:15:56.769 --> 00:15:59.038
Dumas must be making
use of scientists here

00:15:59.038 --> 00:16:01.802
to develop a machine
that opens up the Zone.

00:16:02.141 --> 00:16:04.769
- No, he's done it.
- Let's hurry!

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:09.176
Helga! We have to find that girl
before he does!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.593
At the Ged Group, under the direction
of Gherta Hawksbee,

00:16:20.593 --> 00:16:23.663
a dimension based on the multi-
dimensional theory, the Ged Dimension,

00:16:23.663 --> 00:16:26.928
basically the world after death,
was being researched and developed.

00:16:26.999 --> 00:16:28.694
Yes, those are the King's wishes.

00:16:28.801 --> 00:16:32.605
Oh, Demian, we didn't
know you were here.

00:16:32.605 --> 00:16:36.842
That's right, Professor Gherta,
you've never met before, have you?

00:16:36.842 --> 00:16:39.367
This is Demian from the
Royal Security Agency.

00:16:39.879 --> 00:16:42.515
He's the real power behind this project.

00:16:42.515 --> 00:16:45.746
Yes, I have heard of him.

00:16:46.819 --> 00:16:51.090
I'm sure you've only heard nonsense
about me from these old men,

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.523
Professor Gherta.

00:16:52.625 --> 00:16:53.859
No.

00:16:53.859 --> 00:16:55.661
Without your recommendation,

00:16:55.661 --> 00:16:57.963
this very expensive project

00:16:57.963 --> 00:17:00.989
would never have proceeded
as quickly as it has.

00:17:05.004 --> 00:17:07.234
As a scientist, I am grateful to you.

00:17:26.926 --> 00:17:28.723
Professor Gherta.

00:17:30.663 --> 00:17:35.600
How much longer will it take to
complete the Kuril Island Ring?

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.908
In order to find the place
with the view in that picture,

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:54.943
Helga left the island with Chitto.

00:17:56.922 --> 00:17:59.125
I thought they were my friends.

00:17:59.125 --> 00:18:01.861
I thought I'd be able to help Helga.

00:18:01.861 --> 00:18:04.193
Isn't that right, Mom?!

00:18:06.499 --> 00:18:09.935
That girl has no place to call her own.

00:18:10.369 --> 00:18:12.997
A place where she can
smile from her heart.

00:18:13.706 --> 00:18:17.164
And she might be searching
very hard for that.

00:18:18.644 --> 00:18:20.874
A place to call her own...

00:18:22.281 --> 00:18:24.483
It's that place in her drawings!

00:18:24.483 --> 00:18:26.485
Mom, Dad...

00:18:26.485 --> 00:18:29.455
I want to help Helga!

00:18:29.455 --> 00:18:31.923
I want to look for that place with her!

00:18:34.226 --> 00:18:36.162
We understand, Thoma.

00:18:36.162 --> 00:18:39.064
But in return,
since this is your decision,

00:18:39.064 --> 00:18:42.522
no matter what happens,
don't lose heart! Okay?

00:18:43.736 --> 00:18:47.263
Thoma! Be careful!

00:18:57.049 --> 00:19:00.815
Helga! Chitto!

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.554
Helga!

00:19:11.063 --> 00:19:12.655
Wonder!

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:21.106
Thoma, who had set out from
the island in search of Helga,

00:19:21.106 --> 00:19:22.767
was swallowed up by the waves.

00:19:23.042 --> 00:19:24.410
Damn it!
You jerk!

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.111
-Let go of me!
-We saved Thoma,

00:19:26.111 --> 00:19:28.477
-You're also...
-and decided to work together.

00:19:28.581 --> 00:19:30.879
You're also searching
for Helga, aren't you?

00:19:33.652 --> 00:19:36.780
She's a very special person to us.

00:19:37.122 --> 00:19:39.992
In the same way that
she's special to you.

00:19:39.992 --> 00:19:43.189
You people...
Who are you anyway?!

00:19:44.163 --> 00:19:47.030
What do you intend to do to Helga?!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.202
We'll tell you our reasons later.

00:19:50.202 --> 00:19:52.762
Will you search for her with us?

00:19:52.938 --> 00:19:56.931
Helga! Her boat might
have capsized! Hurry up!

00:19:59.612 --> 00:20:01.680
Helga! Chitto!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:04.183
-Thoma!
-Don't "Thoma" me!

00:20:04.183 --> 00:20:06.185
I've been worried, Chitto!

00:20:06.185 --> 00:20:08.119
I'm sorry.

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:13.957
Anyway, I'm glad you're okay.

00:20:14.126 --> 00:20:16.424
Who are those guys?!

00:20:28.908 --> 00:20:30.603
You're Helga, right?

00:20:32.211 --> 00:20:36.147
We've been looking for you
for a long time.

00:20:40.519 --> 00:20:46.959
Helga, your real name is that of the
daughter of Titus, king of Greecia...

00:20:46.959 --> 00:20:48.449
Tina!

00:20:50.596 --> 00:20:55.192
That day, a tragedy occured
on the planet of Greecia.

00:20:56.402 --> 00:21:00.463
The palace was destroyed to the
point that the ground was torn apart.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.899
And we...

00:21:04.076 --> 00:21:07.580
Tina, in order to save your soul,

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.149
with the soul transference
device we had created,

00:21:10.149 --> 00:21:14.609
the Out Zone, we sent your soul
to this planet.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.081
At our own discretion.

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.559
No matter what our reasons,

00:21:20.559 --> 00:21:22.494
as scientists, we had
taken a course of action

00:21:22.494 --> 00:21:24.894
we couldn't take back.

00:21:27.166 --> 00:21:29.134
In order to go after Tina,

00:21:29.134 --> 00:21:32.938
using the coordinates of the place
we'd transfered her as our destination,

00:21:32.938 --> 00:21:34.940
what in Earth time was
more than 500 years ago,

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.238
we transfered ourselves to Earth.

00:21:39.211 --> 00:21:42.581
To find your soul,
and at the very least,

00:21:42.581 --> 00:21:45.049
send it back to Greecia's Zone.

00:21:49.154 --> 00:21:52.783
The planet... Greecia.

00:22:08.707 --> 00:22:11.403
A little longer, Big Sister.

00:22:11.944 --> 00:22:16.472
Just a little longer, and I'll be
able to bring you back to life.

00:22:34.299 --> 00:22:44.106
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:44.376 --> 00:22:54.219
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:54.219 --> 00:22:58.952
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:22:58.991 --> 00:23:03.826
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:04.229 --> 00:23:13.365
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:13.472 --> 00:23:18.544
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:18.544 --> 00:23:23.816
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:23.816 --> 00:23:28.219
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:28.253 --> 00:23:32.558
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:32.558 --> 00:23:37.427
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
